@startuml Database Layer Detail

title Expense Tracker - Database Layer (Esquema de Base de Datos y Relaciones)

!theme plain

entity "users" as users {
    * id : INTEGER <<PK>>
    --
    * email : VARCHAR(255) <<UNIQUE>>
    * password_hash : VARCHAR(255)
    first_name : VARCHAR(100)
    last_name : VARCHAR(100)
    created_at : DATETIME
    updated_at : DATETIME
}

entity "categories" as categories {
    * id : INTEGER <<PK>>
    --
    * name : VARCHAR(100)
    description : TEXT
    color : VARCHAR(7)
    icon : VARCHAR(50)
    user_id : INTEGER <<FK>>
    is_default : BOOLEAN
    created_at : DATETIME
    updated_at : DATETIME
}

entity "expenses" as expenses {
    * id : INTEGER <<PK>>
    --
    * amount : DECIMAL(10,2)
    * description : TEXT
    * date : DATE
    * category_id : INTEGER <<FK>>
    * user_id : INTEGER <<FK>>
    receipt_filename : VARCHAR(255)
    tags : TEXT
    notes : TEXT
    created_at : DATETIME
    updated_at : DATETIME
}

users ||--o{ expenses : "has many"
users ||--o{ categories : "has many"
categories ||--o{ expenses : "categorizes"

note right of expenses
Performance Indexes:
- idx_expenses_user_id ON (user_id)
- idx_expenses_date ON (date)  
- idx_expenses_category_id ON (category_id)

Query Optimization:
- Composite index for user_id + date
- Full-text search on description + notes
- Category filtering optimization
end note

note right of categories
Performance Indexes:
- idx_categories_user_id ON (user_id)

Category Types:
- System categories (user_id = NULL, is_default = TRUE)
- User categories (user_id = user.id, is_default = FALSE)

Default Categories:
- Food & Dining, Transportation, Shopping
- Entertainment, Bills & Utilities, Healthcare
- Travel, Education
end note

note left of users
Authentication Features:
- Unique email constraint
- bcrypt password hashing
- JWT token-based auth
- Soft delete capability

User Data:
- Profile information
- Account creation tracking  
- Last login tracking (future)
- Preferences storage (future)
end note

class "connection.js" as Connection
class "database.js" as Config
class "schema.sql" as Schema
class "seed.sql" as Seed
class "seeder.js" as Seeder

class "SQLite3" as SQLite
class "PostgreSQL" as PostgreSQL
class "Knex.js" as Knex

Connection --> Knex : uses query builder
Config --> Connection : configures
Schema ..> users : creates
Schema ..> categories : creates  
Schema ..> expenses : creates
Seed ..> categories : populates default
Seeder --> Seed : executes

SQLite --> Connection : development
PostgreSQL --> Connection : production

note bottom of Knex
Knex.js Features:
- Cross-database compatibility
- Query builder with SQL generation
- Migration management
- Connection pooling
- Transaction support
- Promise-based interface

Configuration:
- SQLite3 for development
- PostgreSQL for production
- Connection retry logic
- Query logging in dev mode
end note

note bottom of expenses
Data Constraints:
- Amount must be positive decimal
- Date cannot be in the future
- Category must exist and be accessible
- User must own the expense
- Receipt filename length limit
- Tags array max 10 items
- Notes max 1000 characters

Business Rules:
- Users can only see their own expenses
- Default categories available to all users
- Custom categories private to owner
- Soft delete preserves referential integrity
end note

@enduml